WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.680
A country house.

2
00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:06.490
In an ornate cabinet, one
drawer stands open, and empty.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.960
Footprints cross a nearby beach.

4
00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:12.720
Then a cab draws up, and
out steps a thin man,

5
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:14.180
all in black.

6
00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:17.010
"He might have been a
parson, or an undertaker,

7
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.850
or anything else you like,
except what he really was."

8
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.030
Whodunit?

9
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.280
Every crime story asks that.

10
00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.360
But what else is it asking?

11
00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:30.070
In this mission, you'll
find two stories inside one:

12
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.520
the crime, hidden in the past,
and the investigation we read.

13
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:37.040
You'll watch the detective as an outsider,

14
00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.270
reading clues that others miss.

15
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:43.300
And you'll ask whether one crime
can point back to an older one.

16
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:47.410
Your mission: work out what
else a crime story is asking.
